# Derived from CatalaLang/catala tests/exception/good/unsorted_unlabeled_exceptions.catala_en
# Copyright (c) Inria and the Catala contributors. Apache-2.0.
# Modified: re-expressed in Payment Charter DSL.
#
# Catala writes the exceptions before the definitions they attach to and
# answers the same as if they had been written after: source order is not
# meaning.
#
# Charter agrees for its own reason. §5.2 makes declarations order-independent
# and resolves names in a pass separate from parsing, so the limit below may be
# written before the asset it spends. §1.2's canonical form then sorts both, so
# the emitted document does not record which order the author typed.
charter unsorted version 1
resolver common@41
timezone UTC

  limit spend
    amount 100.00 USDC_circle
    per fixed day

  asset USDC_circle = mint://USDC/Circle/EPjFWdd5AufqSSqeM2qN1xzybapC8G4wEGGkZwyTDt1v/solana:5eykt4UsFv8P8NJdTREpY1vzqKqZKvdp
